; Samples the ten inputs at each falling edge of a pin: an Amiga drive's
; select (fdd_step does STEP). An Amiga selects its drive for a few microseconds
; at a time (32 pulses of 4 us to read a drive's ID; 20 us around each step)
; and changes DIR with the select, so core 1's once-a-pass sample may miss a
; pulse, or see DIR as it was after. Each sample here is the inputs as they
; were within two cycles of the edge.
;
; Configure: jmp pin = the edge's pin; IN base = the first input (GPIO 12),
; shifting left, no autopush; RX FIFO joined (8 samples). A full FIFO drops
; the newest sample (push noblock): core 1 drains it every pass.

.program fdd_edge

.wrap_target
low:
    jmp pin high        ; wait for the pin to be high (released)
    jmp low
high:
    jmp pin high        ; then for it to fall
    in pins, 10         ; GPIO 12-21 at the edge
    push noblock
.wrap
